---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import ToolCard from '../../components/ToolCard.astro';
import { tools } from '../../lib/tools';
const matching = tools.filter((tool) => tool.sourceLicense === 'Open Source' && tool.standards.includes('UML'));
---

<MainLayout title="Open-Source UML Tools — NeoMBSE" description="Explore open-source UML tools while distinguishing the software license, hosted service, tool type, and modeling interface.">
  <article class="section container">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">License guide</p><h1>Open-source UML tools.</h1></div><p class="lead">Compare editors and diagram generators without treating every “free” offer as the same licensing model.</p></div>
    <div class="callout"><strong>Catalog note:</strong> licensing models can change between product versions and editions. Check the vendor’s current terms before making a decision.</div>
    <div class="tool-grid">{matching.map((tool) => <ToolCard tool={tool} />)}</div>
    <div class="guide-copy prose narrow">
      <h2>Open source is only one selection dimension</h2>
      <p>The application license, hosted service, plugin ecosystem, and enterprise extensions may use different commercial models. NeoMBSE records these separately wherever the evidence allows.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</MainLayout>

<style>.guide-copy { margin: 5rem 0 0; }</style>
